 ## Standing state
 
 - Greenfield build of TodoMVC (Vanilla JS, no preprocessors, localStorage persistence).
-- Harness bootstrapped: `package.json` with `@cucumber/cucumber` + `happy-dom`, `features/support/world.js` loads real `index.html` + `js/app.js` into happy-dom per-scenario, disposes after. Routing patched to fire `hashchange` on click.
-- Assets landed: `assets/app-spec.md` (product spec), `assets/app-template.index.html` (base markup).
-- Durable work this cycle: spec feature files under `features/`, `watchbill.json`.
+- Harness: Cucumber + happy-dom, loads real index.html + js/app.js per-scenario.
+- 42 scenarios: 39 behaviour scenarios pass, 3 @contract scenarios (1 storage shape, 2 conformance).
+- Assets: `assets/app-spec.md` (product spec), `assets/app-template.index.html` (base markup).
+
+## Defects found via external browser acceptance suite (Cypress)
+
+### 1. DOM Detachment (affects toggle/toggle-all/completed state changes)
+
+- **Cause**: `render()` in `js/app.js` calls `todoList.innerHTML = ''` then rebuilds every `<li>` from scratch. In a real browser, any reference Cypress held to a DOM node before the interaction is invalidated after re-render.
+- **Evidence**: 4 Cypress failures on "Mark all as completed" and individual toggling — `cy.eq()/cy.find() failed because the page updated as a result of this command... element is no longer attached to the DOM`.
+- **Existing in-harness coverage**: The toggle scenarios pass because happy-dom does not track element identity across re-renders. A source-level conformance check captures this.
+- **Fix**: Mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place — toggle `.completed` class on the parent `<li>`, toggle `.toggle` checkbox `checked` property, instead of destroying and recreating elements. Applies to:
+  - Individual toggle checkbox click handler
+  - Toggle-all click handler
+  - Any other state change that currently triggers full re-render
+
+### 2. Editing Mode Broken (affects dblclick → edit input visibility)
+
+- **Cause**: The dblclick handler sets `todo.editing = true` then calls `render()`. `render()` begins with `todos = getTodos()` which reads from localStorage — but `editing` is never persisted to localStorage. So the in-memory flag is discarded, the new `<li>` never gets `.editing` class, and the edit input stays `display: none`.
+- **Evidence**: 6 Cypress failures on editing operations — `cy.clear()/cy.type() failed because element has CSS property: display: none` and `expected '<label>' not to be 'visible'`.
+- **Existing in-harness coverage**: The editing step definition in `steps.js` bypasses the real dblclick handler by writing `editing: true` directly into localStorage before dispatching hashchange. This means the test passes even though the app's actual dblclick handler is broken. A source-level conformance check captures this.
+- **Fix approach A**: Keep transient state (editing) in a separate in-memory map or pass current todos to `render()` instead of re-reading from localStorage.
+- **Fix approach B (preferred)**: Mutate the existing `<li>` in place on dblclick — add `.editing` class to the `<li>`, show the `.edit` input, hide the `.view`, without calling full `render()`.
 
 ## Decisions
 
-- Storage key: `todos-vanillajs` per spec convention (`todos-[framework]`).
-- Tier: happy-dom (default). The spec requires DOM rendering; happy-dom is the cheapest tier that observes it.
-- Scantling for localStorage shape at `scantlings/todo-storage.json`.
+- Both defects share the same root cause: `render()` is a destructive full rebuild. The proper fix is to switch to in-place DOM mutation for state changes, only calling a full render on initial load or after a wholesale change (filter switch, clear completed).
+- The spec (`assets/app-spec.md`) already describes the correct behaviour — the implementation diverges.
+- Conformance checks are @contract scenarios that read `js/app.js` source and reject the anti-patterns. They fail on current code.
+- watchbill.json created with two targets: DOM-DETACHMENT and EDITING-BROKEN.
 
